{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc && sed -n '110,180p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc && sed -n '700,790p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc && sed -n '200,340p' test/yang/python/antlr/siteset_test.cljc && cat .git\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.python.antlr.dht-import-fixture\n  \"The JVM publication artifact of C4 slice I3's DHT import\n   (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): test/resources/yang/python/\n   dht-import-v1.edn, written on the JVM by\n   test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.generate.clj.\n\n   It holds what a publisher `A` publishes and signs: the guest blobs of\n   the units m, k, t and e and of k's republication k2 (every blob of\n   their closures but `py`'s, which each reader has installed, and each\n   module's site set blob and publication record blob, I7), each\n   unit's manifest address, the signed name envelopes of three index\n   transactions -- `A` naming py, yang.call, m, k and t; `A` retracting k and\n   naming k2; a foreign principal `B` naming e -- and the importer\n   packets the reader lowers, and a fourth index transaction of `A`'s signed\n   site-set publication entries (I7). The keys are fixed test seeds, and Ed25519\n   signatures are deterministic, so one host's `generate` is the file\n   byte for byte.\n\n   `yang.python.antlr.dht-import-test` consumes the file on every host\n   without republishing anything, and checks that this host's own\n   `generate` equals it: a host whose publication of the same packets\n   differs from the JVM's fails there.\n\n   One EDN form per line: the magic, the header maps, then one\n   `[address hex]` line per blob in address order.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.jing :as jing]\n    [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as cfx]\n    [dao.jing.dht :as jing.dht]\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.python.antlr.import-programs :as programs]\n    [yang.python.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n    [yang.python.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.python.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yin.vm.linker.closure :as closure]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n\n\n(def path\n  \"The artifact, relative to the repository root.\"\n  \"test/resources/yang/python/dht-import-v1.edn\")\n\n\n(def magic \"dht-import-v1\")\n\n\n(def key-a\n  \"The publisher `A`: a fixed test seed.\"\n  (let [seed (apply str (repeat 32 \"a1\"))]\n    {:seed seed, :public (sign/public-of seed)}))\n\n\n(def key-b\n  \"The foreign principal `B`: a fixed test seed.\"\n  (let [seed (apply str (repeat 32 \"b2\"))]\n    {:seed seed, :public (sign/public-of seed)}))\n\n\n(defn closure-addresses\n  \"Every blob address of the closure of `manifest` in `store`: the reads\n   one closure walk makes.\"\n  [store manifest]\n  (let [seen (atom #{})\n        get-bytes (:get-bytes-fn store)\n        recording (assoc store\n                         :get-bytes-fn\n                         (fn [address not-found]\n                           (swap! seen conj address)\n                           (get-bytes address not-found)))]\n    (closure/walk recording manifest)\n    @seen))\n\n\n(defn installed-py\n  \"`py`'s closure as this host published it, `{address bytes}`: the\n   Python runtime every reader has installed. It does not travel: three\n   of its blobs (the code images, about 1 MB each) exceed the DHT's\n   64 KiB message bound, which a `dao.space.dht` node does not let a\n   composition raise.\"\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [store address]} @h/published]\n    (select-keys ((:entries-fn store)) (closure-addresses store address))))\n\n\n(defn installed-pysp\n  \"`pysp`'s closure as this host published it, `{address bytes}`: the hook\n   runtime a reader under a hook profile has installed, as it has `py`\n   (the closure includes `py`'s).\"\n  []\n  (let [{:keys [store]} @h/published\n        pysp (:address @h/published-pysp)\n        addresses (closure-addresses store pysp)]\n    (select-keys ((:entries-fn store)) addresses)))\n\n\n(defn- unit\n  [nm pk]\n  {:name nm, :packet pk, :package? false})\n\n\n(defn- assert-names\n  \"`key`'s assertions binding each `[module address]` of `bound`, at\n   consecutive sequences from `seq0`.\"\n  [key seq0 bound]\n  (vec (map-indexed (fn [i [n a]]\n                      (publish/assertion key {:name n,\n                                              :manifest a,\n                                              :seq (+ seq0 i)}))\n                    bound)))\n\n\n(defn- signed-only\n  [signed]\n  (mapv #(select-keys % [:envelope :proof]) signed))\n\n\n(defn generate\n  \"This host's artifact: the units published from the committed packets\n   into a store holding `py` as this host published it, `A`'s and `B`'s\n   envelopes signed over the addresses. Answers `{:lines [...]}`, or the\n   first publication refusal as `{:refused r}`.\"\n  []\n  (let [py (:address @h/published)\n        installed (installed-py)\n        store (mem/create-content-mem installed)\n        units (publication/publish-units!\n                store (h/registry) py\n                [(unit \"m\" programs/m-packet) (unit \"k\" programs/k-packet)\n                 (unit \"t\" programs/t-packet) (unit \"e\" programs/e-packet)])\n        k2 (publication/publish-units! store (h/registry) py\n                                       [(unit \"k\" programs/k2-packet)])]\n    (if-let [refused (some #(when (not= :ok (:status %)) %) [units k2])]\n      {:refused refused}\n      (let [addresses (:addresses units)\n            own (assert-names key-a 1 [['py py]\n                                       ['yang.call (:call-address @h/published)]\n                                       ['pym.m (get addresses \"m\")]\n                                       ['pym.k (get addresses \"k\")]\n                                       ['pym.t (get addresses \"t\")]])\n            republish [(publish/retraction\n                         key-a\n                         {:of (jing/segment-key (:envelope (nth own 3))),\n                          :seq 6})\n                       (publish/assertion\n                         key-a\n                         {:name 'pym.k,\n                          :manifest (get-in k2 [:addresses \"k\"]),\n                          :seq 7})]\n            foreign (assert-names key-b 1 [['pym.e (get addresses \"e\")]])\n            ;; I7: A's signed publication entry for each module's site-set\n            ;; record, the units' then k's republication\n            sites (into []\n                        (mapcat #(siteset/signed-entries\n                                   key-a (:sites %) (:addresses %)\n                                   (:bundles %)))\n                        [units k2])\n            blobs (sort-by (comp str key)\n                           (remove (fn [[a _]] (contains? installed a))\n                                   ((:entries-fn store))))]\n        {:lines\n         (into [magic\n                (pr-str {:py py})\n                (pr-str {:principals {:a (:public key-a),\n                                      :b (:public key-b)}})\n                (pr-str {:units addresses,\n                         :republished {\"k\" (get-in k2 [:addresses \"k\"])}})\n                (pr-str {:importers {:d programs/d-packet,\n                                     :tt programs/tt-packet,\n                                     :x programs/x-packet}})\n                (pr-str {:index :own, :signed (signed-only own)})\n                (pr-str {:index :republish, :signed (signed-only republish)})\n                (pr-str {:index :foreign, :signed (signed-only foreign)})\n                (pr-str {:index :sites, :signed sites})]\n               (map (fn [[a bs]] (pr-str [a (jing.dht/bytes->hex bs)])))\n               blobs)}))))\n\n\n(defn text\n  \"The artifact text of `lines`: one per line, newline terminated.\"\n  [lines]\n  (str (str/join \"\\n\" lines) \"\\n\"))\n\n\n(defn read-lines\n  \"The artifact's lines, blank ones dropped (Dart keeps a trailing one).\"\n  []\n  (vec (remove str/blank? (str/split-lines (cfx/read-path path)))))\n\n\n(defn parse\n  \"Artifact `lines` as data, `{:py :principals :units :republished\n   :importers :indexes {kind [signed ...]} :blobs {address hex}}`: what\n   two artifacts are compared by, since a host prints a map's entries in\n   its own order.\"\n  [lines]\n  (let [[m & forms] lines]\n    (when-not (= magic m)\n      (throw (ex-info \"not a dht-import-v1 artifact\" {:path path})))\n    (reduce (fn [acc line]\n              (let [form (edn/read-string line)]\n                (cond\n                  (vector? form) (assoc-in acc [:blobs (first form)]\n                                           (second form))\n                  (:index form) (assoc-in acc [:indexes (:index form)]\n                                          (:signed form))\n                  :else (merge acc form))))\n            {:blobs {}, :indexes {}}\n            forms)))\n\n\n(defn read-file\n  \"The checked-in artifact, `parse`'s data with each blob as host\n   bytes.\"\n  []\n  (update (parse (read-lines))\n          :blobs\n          (fn [blobs]\n    (is (= before-addresses\n           (set (keys ((:entries-fn store))))))))\n\n\n;; the artifact's modules as [name manifest]: the units, then k's republication\n(defn- artifact-modules\n  [artifact]\n  (into (vec (sort-by key (:units artifact)))\n        (map (fn [[n m]] [(str n \" (republished)\") m]))\n        (:republished artifact)))\n\n\n(deftest published-site-sets-verify-test\n  (testing \"every module of the artifact has a site-set record that A's\n            signed index entry publishes, discovered from the published\n            code under A alone, fetched by address, and verifying against\n            the manifest in the artifact's own blobs: root, frontend\n            revision, transformation profile and the set's address (C4\n            slice I7)\"\n    (let [artifact (fixture/read-file)\n          store (mem/create-content-mem (:blobs artifact))\n          datoms (siteset/entry-datoms (get-in artifact [:indexes :sites]))\n          {:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n          hooks {:profile :py/hooks, :hooks true}]\n      (doseq [[n manifest] (artifact-modules artifact)]\n        (let [found (siteset/discover datoms [a] manifest)]\n          (is (= 1 (count found)) n)\n          (is (nil? (siteset/verify store manifest (first found))) n)\n          (is (= :ok (:status (siteset/admit store manifest found hooks))) n)\n          (is (= [] (siteset/discover datoms [b] manifest))\n              (str n \" is not discovered under a principal that did not sign it\"))\n          (is (= :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set\n                 (:reason (siteset/admit store manifest [] hooks)))\n              n))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The mesh world: a publisher, two plain peers, a reader\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private big\n  \"Every node's inbound bound: py's closure is replicated whole.\"\n  (* 512 1024 1024))\n\n\n(defn- peer-node\n  [net port]\n  (let [c (mesh/join! net port {::jing.dht/publish? true\n                                ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes big})]\n    {:composition c, :state (jing.dht/state c)}))\n\n\n(defn- node-at\n  \"A node at mesh `port` whose local store already holds `seed`\n   ({address bytes}): content it has, not content it publishes.\"\n  [net port peer-ports publish? seed]\n  (dht/join {:local (mem/create-content-mem seed),\n             :publish? publish?,\n             :peers (mapv (fn [p] {:host mesh/host, :port p}) peer-ports),\n             :bind! (mesh/seam net port),\n             :max-inbound-bytes big}))\n\n\n(defn- step-world\n  \"One reading: the publisher, the reader when there is one, then every\n   plain peer.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [now (:now w)\n        [pub pub-events] (dht/step (:pub w) now)\n        [reader] (when (:reader w) (dht/step (:reader w) now))]\n    (-> w\n\n\n(defn- site-sets-over-the-mesh\n  \"I7's mesh leg: the reader loads `A`'s site-set index and discovers each\n   unit's record address from the entries `A` signed. It holds no record\n   bytes: the stage load of an import fetches them (`hook-import-with-the-\n   index`). Nothing here prefetches.\"\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a]} (:principals artifact)\n        [w m] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :sites]))\n        datoms (dht/loaded-datoms (:reader w) m)\n        modules (remove (fn [[n _]] (= \"e\" n)) (sort-by key (:units artifact)))\n        records (into {}\n                      (map (fn [[n manifest]]\n                             [n (siteset/discover datoms [a] manifest)]))\n                      modules)]\n    (testing \"the reader discovers one record per module from the index\"\n      (is (some? datoms))\n      (is (every? #(= 1 (count (val %))) records) (pr-str records)))\n    (testing \"the reader holds no record before any import\"\n      (is (every? (fn [[_ rs]]\n                    (nil? ((:get-bytes-fn (dht/local (:reader w)))\n                           (first rs) nil)))\n                  records)))\n    w))\n\n\n(defn- hook-source\n  \"The reader's DHT source declaring `A`, trusting `A`, `py` named by `A`'s\n   assertion and `pysp` by a direct entry, composed with the link-time\n   stage of a hook profile (no local records: it discovers them).\"\n  [artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a]} (:principals artifact)\n        pysp (:address @h/published-pysp)]\n    (link/composition\n      {:dht? true,\n       :principals [a],\n       :name-env {'pysp pysp},\n       :admission {:trusted #{(sign/principal a)}},\n       :stage (siteset/stage (h/registry)\n                             {:profile :py/hooks,\n                              :hooks true,\n                              :hooks-profile hooks/linked-profile,\n                              :pysp pysp}\n                             {})})))\n\n\n(defn- noting-waits\n  \"A `between` for `run-over-dht` recording under `:waits` every manifest\n   a pending entry waits on.\"\n  [w served]\n  (-> w\n      (update :waits (fnil into #{}) (keep :manifest (:pending served)))\n      (update :responses (fnil into #{})\n              (map #(dissoc % :yin.link/id :image)\n                   (mesh/values (:responses (:pair served)))))))\n\n\n(defn- hook-import-refused-without-the-index\n  \"Without `A`'s site-set index loaded the reader's stage finds no record:\n   the import is refused at link time naming the profile and the set, with\n   nothing fetched.\"\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [m (get-in artifact [:units \"m\"])\n        [w outcome response _]\n        (run-over-dht w :semantic (get-in artifact [:importers :d])\n                      (hook-source artifact) (fn [w _] w) {:signals []})]\n    (testing \"no site-set index: refused, the importer ends with ImportError\"\n      (is (= \"ImportError\" (get-in (nth outcome 2) [:py/exception :type]))\n          (pr-str outcome))\n      (is (= :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set (:reason response))\n          (pr-str response))\n      (is (= :py/hooks (:profile response)))\n      (is (= 'pym.m (:name response)))\n      (is (= m (:yin.link/canonical response))))\n    w))\n\n\n(defn- hook-import-with-the-index\n  \"With `A`'s site-set index loaded the cold reader's stage load fetches\n   m's record and set by address, derives and delivers the instrumented\n   module; the program runs.\"\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a]} (:principals artifact)\n        m (get-in artifact [:units \"m\"])\n        record (first (siteset/discover\n                        (into []\n                              (mapcat #(ld/snapshot-datoms (:reader w) %))\n                              (ld/snapshots (:reader w)))\n                        [a] m))\n        [w outcome response seen]\n    (testing \"a discovered record admits\"\n      (is (= :ok (:status (siteset/admit\n                            store manifest\n                            (siteset/discover datoms [(:public key-a)] manifest)\n                            requirement)))))))\n\n\n(defn- stub-store\n  \"A store holding stand-in `yang.call`, `py` and `pysp` modules (the\n   stage reads the hook module's manifest for the derived footprint):\n   `[store py pysp]`.\"\n  []\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        stub (fn [nm requires]\n               (:address (publish/publish-module!\n                           store {:name nm, :ast (u/lit nil), :exports #{},\n                                  :requires requires, :primitives {}})))\n        call (stub 'yang.call {})\n        py (stub 'py {'yang.call call})\n        pysp (stub 'pysp {'py py})]\n    [store py pysp]))\n\n\n(defn- hook-requirement\n  [pysp]\n  (assoc requirement\n         :hooks-profile hooks/linked-profile\n         :pysp pysp))\n\n\n(defn- records-of\n  \"`{manifest [record-address]}` for the publication `result`.\"\n  [result]\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [[n s]]\n               [(get (:addresses result) n) [(:record-address s)]]))\n        (:sites result)))\n\n\n(def ^:private no-datoms\n  {:datoms [], :principals []})\n\n\n(deftest an-scc-member-alias-carries-no-set-test\n  (let [[store py pysp] (stub-store)\n        result (publication/publish-units!\n                 store (h/registry) py\n                 [{:name \"ca\", :packet programs/ca-packet}\n                  {:name \"cb\", :packet programs/cb-packet}])\n        bundle (get (:bundles result) 'pyscc.ca$$cb)\n        alias-a (get (:addresses result) \"ca\")\n        bundle-site (get (:sites result) 'pyscc.ca$$cb)\n        ctx (assoc no-datoms :store store)]\n    (is (= :ok (:status result)) (pr-str result))\n    (testing \"the marks are in the bundle, which carries the set\"\n      (is (seq (:set bundle-site)))\n      (is (nil? (siteset/verify store bundle (:record-address bundle-site))))\n      (is (= :ok (:status (siteset/admit store bundle\n                                         [(:record-address bundle-site)]\n                                         requirement)))))\n    (testing \"an alias has no marks and no set\"\n      (is (not (contains? (:sites result) \"ca\")))\n      (is (not (contains? (:sites result) \"cb\"))))\n    (testing \"a member import under a hook profile is refused by the stage,\n              not run uninstrumented under the lie of an empty set\"\n      (let [out ((siteset/stage (h/registry) (hook-requirement pysp) {})\n                 ctx 'pym.ca alias-a)]\n        (is (= :refused (:status out)))\n        (is (= :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set (:reason out)))\n        (is (contains? siteset/reasons (:reason out)))\n        (is (= 'pym.ca (:name out)))\n        (is (= :py/hooks (:profile out)))))\n    (testing \"a noninterruptible profile imports the alias as published\"\n      (is (= {:status :ok, :address alias-a}\n             (select-keys ((siteset/stage (h/registry)\n                                          {:profile :py/plain,\n                                           :noninterruptible true}\n                                          {})\n                           ctx 'pym.ca alias-a)\n                          [:status :address]))))\n    (is (some? bundle))))\n\n\n(deftest the-stage-answers-the-derive-record-test\n  (let [[store py pysp] (stub-store)\n        result (publication/publish-units!\n                 store (h/registry) py\n                 [{:name \"w\", :packet loops/while-true-pass}])\n        manifest (get (:addresses result) \"w\")\n        ctx (assoc no-datoms :store store)\n        out ((siteset/stage (h/registry) (hook-requirement pysp)\n                            (records-of result))\n             ctx 'pym.w manifest)\n        record (jing/get store (:derivation out) nil)\n        selected (filter (fn [[_ mark]]\n                           (#{:loop :call} (if (vector? mark) (first mark) mark)))\n                         (:set (get (:sites result) \"w\")))\n        sites-address (jing/segment-key (safepoint/site-set selected))]\n    (is (= :ok (:status out)) (pr-str out))\n    (is (not= manifest (:address out)))\n    (testing \"the :derive record is materialized and answered\"\n      (is (= :derive (:yin.ledger/op record)))\n      (is (= :yang.safepoint/insert (:yin.ledger/function record)))\n      (is (= (:yin.module/tree (jing/get store manifest nil))\n             (:yin.ledger/input record)))\n      (is (= (:yin.module/tree (jing/get store (:address out) nil))\n             (:yin.ledger/output record)))\n      (is (= {:yang.safepoint/hooks hooks/linked-profile,\n              :yang.safepoint/sites sites-address}\n             (:yin.ledger/profile record))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-dependency-with-no-set-refuses-the-chain-test\n  (let [[store py pysp] (stub-store)\n        result (publication/publish-units!\n                 store (h/registry) py\n                 [{:name \"k\", :packet programs/k-packet}\n                  {:name \"t\", :packet programs/t-packet}])\n        records (records-of result)\n        t (get (:addresses result) \"t\")\n        k (get (:addresses result) \"k\")\n        stage (siteset/stage (h/registry) (hook-requirement pysp)\n                             (dissoc records k))\n        out (stage (assoc no-datoms :store store) 'pym.t t)]\n    (is (= :ok (:status ((siteset/stage (h/registry) (hook-requirement pysp)\n                                        records)\n                         (assoc no-datoms :store store) 'pym.t t))))\n    (is (= :refused (:status out)))\n    (is (= :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set (:reason out)))\n    (is (= 'pym.k (:name out)))\n    (is (= t (:via out)))))\n\n\n(deftest the-stage-writes-nothing-until-it-can-complete-test\n  (let [[store py pysp] (stub-store)\n        result (publication/publish-units!\n                 store (h/registry) py\n                 [{:name \"k\", :packet loops/while-true-pass}\n                  {:name \"t\", :packet programs/t-packet}])\n        records (records-of result)\n        t (get (:addresses result) \"t\")\ngitdir: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.git/worktrees/datomworld-hk\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"k-packet|defn.*k|:hooks|:noninterruptible|runtime\\\" test/yang/python/antlr/import_programs.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc && sed -n '1,130p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc && sed -n '360,530p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc && sed -n '530,710p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"k-packet|defn.*k|:hooks|:noninterruptible|runtime\\\" test/yang/python/antlr/import_programs.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc && sed -n '1,130p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc && sed -n '360,530p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc && sed -n '530,710p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:79:   Python runtime every reader has installed. It does not travel: three\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:90:   runtime a reader under a hook profile has installed, as it has `py`\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc:131:                [(unit \"m\" programs/m-packet) (unit \"k\" programs/k-packet)\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:19:   `py` is the runtime every node has installed, one manifest address on\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:84:             [(unit \"t\" programs/t-packet) (unit \"k\" programs/k-packet)\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:133:          hooks {:profile :py/hooks, :hooks true}]\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:250:  \"The lines the Python runtime of `task` has printed, read off its\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:451:   child; `yang.call` and `py` are the two runtime install children.\"\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:661:(defn- an-allow-binds-the-address-the-question-was-asked-about\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:727:(defn- hook-source\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:741:                              :hooks true,\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:742:                              :hooks-profile hooks/linked-profile,\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:758:(defn- hook-import-refused-without-the-index\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:778:(defn- hook-import-with-the-index\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:810:(defn- a-hook-import-chain\nsrc/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc:9:   runtime call path uses that dispatcher.\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_programs.cljc:182:(def k-packet\n(ns yang.python.antlr.publication\n  \"C4 slices I3 and I5 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): a set of compiled Python\n   units published as linker modules. The ordering, SCC bundling and publish\n   loop are `yang.core.publication`'s; this namespace supplies the Python\n   hooks: the imports `lower/imported-module-names` hoists, the\n   `lower/module-spec` and `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters, the I7 site\n   set, and no binder table. Every Python module pins the `yang.call`\n   address from the published `py` module's requirements because its\n   runtime call path uses that dispatcher.\n   Name assertions stay the linker's (`yin.vm.linker.publish/assertion`\n   and `name-envelopes`): this namespace publishes content, it signs\n   nothing.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.core.publication :as core]\n            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.python.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(defn- unit-imports\n  \"The Python modules unit `u` statically imports.\"\n  [{:keys [name package? packet]}]\n  (lower/imported-module-names packet\n                               {:name name, :package? (boolean package?)}))\n\n\n(defn- config\n  [publish-fn call-address]\n  {:imported-names unit-imports,\n   :module-spec (fn [registry {:keys [name package? packet]} py-address deps]\n                  (lower/module-spec registry packet\n                                     {:name name, :package? package?,\n                                      :py-address py-address, :call-address call-address,\n                                      :deps deps})),\n   :scc-module-specs (fn [registry units py-address deps]\n                       (lower/scc-module-specs registry units py-address call-address deps)),\n   :site-set siteset/publish!,\n   :binder-table nil,\n   :refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\",\n   :publish-fn publish-fn})\n\n\n(defn publication-order\n  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the I3 order for acyclic units.\n   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n   publication step per SCC. External imports must be in `published`.\"\n  [units published]\n  (core/publication-order (config publish/publish-module! nil) units published))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"Publish `units` (`[{:name :package? :packet}]`) into the content store\n   `handle` over the host registry `registry`, `py` pinned at\n   `py-address` and each import outside the set at its address in\n   `published` ({python-name address}), in `publication-order`. Answers\n   `{:status :ok :addresses {python-name address}\n     :bundles {bundle-symbol address}\n     :sites {python-name-or-bundle-symbol site-publication}}` for the units\n   of the set (`siteset/publish!`'s answer for each module published beside\n   its code image, I7; an SCC member alias carries no marks and so no\n   entry, its bundle does). The publisher that asserts these names\n   indexes `siteset/signed-entries` of `:sites` in the same index\n   transaction; a module whose entry is missing is refused by every\n   hook-profile reader. Or the\n   first refusal: `publication-order`'s before anything is written, else\n   `publish-module!`'s with a string `:unit`: the Python name for a member,\n   or the bundle module name for an SCC bundle. Every bundle name must be\n   asserted/bound alongside the member names for aliases to deliver.\n   Optional `publish-fn` takes `[handle spec]`, defaulting to\n   `publish/publish-module!`, for both bundles and members.\"\n  ([handle registry py-address units]\n   (publish-units! handle registry py-address units {}))\n  ([handle registry py-address units published]\n   (publish-units! handle registry py-address units published publish/publish-module!))\n  ([handle registry py-address units published publish-fn]\n   (let [py-manifest (when (and handle py-address)\n                       (jing/get handle py-address nil))\n         call-address (get-in py-manifest [:yin.module/requires 'yang.call])]\n     (core/publish-units! (config publish-fn call-address)\n                          handle registry py-address units published))))\n                    admission\n                    (if admitted (:interpreter admitted) interp)))\n\n           :else\n           [w\n            [(vm/halted? task) (vm/blocked? task)\n             (render/output (vm/value task))]\n            response\n            (observed task)]))))))\n\n\n(defn- source\n  \"The reader's DHT link source declaring the public keys `publics`, its\n   in-process admission interpreter trusting the principals of the\n   public keys `trusted` -- none in process when `trusted` is nil.\"\n  [publics trusted]\n  (link/composition\n    {:dht? true,\n     :principals publics,\n     :admission (when trusted\n                  {:trusted (set (map sign/principal trusted))})}))\n\n\n(defn- on-every-vm\n  \"Thread `w` through `run-over-dht` on every vector backend: `[w {backend\n   [outcome last-response observation]}]`.\"\n  [w pk src]\n  (reduce (fn [[w acc] k]\n            (let [[w outcome response seen] (run-over-dht w k pk src)]\n              [w (assoc acc k [outcome response seen])]))\n          [w {}]\n          (keys h/backends)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The acceptance\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- first-difference\n  \"The first key of the artifacts `a` and `b` (`fixture/parse`'s data)\n   whose values differ, with the blob addresses only one holds or holds\n   other bytes at; nil when they are equal.\"\n  [a b]\n  (when (not= a b)\n    (let [blobs (fn [x y]\n                  (sort (map str (remove #(= (get x %) (get y %))\n                                         (keys x)))))]\n      {:keys (vec (sort (map str (filter #(not= (get a %) (get b %))\n                                         (distinct (concat (keys a)\n                                                           (keys b))))))),\n       :blobs-differ (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs a) (:blobs b)))),\n       :blobs-only-here (vec (take 4 (blobs (:blobs b) (:blobs a))))})))\n\n\n(defn- this-host-publishes-the-artifact\n  [artifact-lines]\n  (testing \"this host's own publication of the committed packets is the\n            JVM's artifact: same manifests, blobs and envelopes\"\n    (let [{:keys [lines refused]} (fixture/generate)]\n      (is (nil? refused) (pr-str refused))\n      (when lines\n        (is (nil? (first-difference (fixture/parse artifact-lines)\n                                    (fixture/parse lines))))))))\n\n\n(defn- publish-world\n  \"Publisher `A` at mesh port 1, plain peers at 2 and 3, a reader at 4,\n   `A` and the reader with `py` installed: `A`'s node serves the\n   artifact's guest blobs as they are and its first index (py, m, k and\n   t named by `A`), which the reader loads.\"\n  [artifact]\n  (let [net (mesh/mesh)\n        installed (fixture/installed-py)\n        pub (node-at net 1 [2 3] true installed)\n        put! (:put-bytes-fn (dht/store pub))\n        w {:net net,\n           :pub pub,\n           :reader (node-at net 4 [2 3 1] false\n                            (merge installed (fixture/installed-pysp))),\n           :peers (into {} (map (fn [p] [p (peer-node net p)])) [2 3]),\n           :now 0,\n           :events []}]\n    (testing \"every node's installed py is the artifact's\"\n      (is (= (:py artifact) (:address @h/published))))\n    (run! (fn [[address bs]] (put! address bs))\n          (sort-by (comp str key) (:blobs artifact)))\n    (first (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :own])))))\n\n\n(def ^:private nothing-ran\n  \"A refused import's observation: no line printed and no guest install\n   child; `yang.call` and `py` are the two runtime install children.\"\n  {:output [], :guests #{}, :children 2})\n\n\n(defn- observes\n  \"Assert each key of the observation `expected` of backend `k` on its\n   own, so a failure names the key.\"\n  [k expected seen]\n  (doseq [[key v] expected]\n    (is (= v (get seen key)) (str k \" \" key))))\n\n\n(defn- imports-over-the-dht\n  [w artifact src]\n  (testing \"a JVM-published pym.m imports over the DHT, parserless, with\n            the in-store linked run's output and CPython's\"\n    (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :d]) src)]\n      (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n        (is (= [true false {:py/out [\"m-body\" \"7\"], :py/exception nil}]\n               outcome)\n            (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n        (testing \"and the observation sees the same run\"\n          ;; The linked task installs `py`, the shared `yang.call`\n          ;; dispatcher, then the guest module.\n          (observes k {:output [\"m-body\" \"7\"], :guests #{\"pym.m\"},\n                       :children 3}\n                    seen)))\n      (testing \"and t delivers k, its pinned import, by name\"\n        (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :tt])\n                                       src)]\n          (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n            (is (= [true false\n                    {:py/out [\"k-body\" \"t-sees 3\" \"t-done\"],\n                     :py/exception nil}]\n                   outcome)\n                (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n            (observes k {:guests #{\"pym.k\" \"pym.t\"}} seen))\n          w)))))\n\n\n(defn- republished-dependency-is-refused\n  [w artifact src]\n  (let [k1 (get-in artifact [:units \"k\"])\n        k2 (get-in artifact [:republished \"k\"])\n        [w _] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :republish]))]\n    (testing \"a republished dependency: t pinned k's first address, k now\n              names another; the link server delivers k2, but the engine\n              refuses receive as a pin mismatch, raising ImportError in t\"\n      (is (not= k1 k2))\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :tt])\n                                     src)]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= [true false\n                  {:py/out [],\n                   :py/exception\n                   {:type \"ImportError\",\n                    :args [\"Cannot import module 'k': linker refused delivery\"]}}]\n                 outcome)\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str outcome)))\n          (is (= {:status :ok,\n                  :yin.admit/address k2}\n                 (select-keys response [:status :yin.admit/address]))\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n          (observes k {:output [], :guests #{\"pym.t\"}, :children 4} seen))\n        w))))\n\n\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n;; B's module: refused untrusted, allowed trusted, bound to its question\n;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n(def ^:private caught-e\n  \"x's run once e is linked: e.boom raises, x catches it.\"\n  [true false {:py/out [\"caught-e\"], :py/exception nil}])\n\n\n(defn- an-untrusted-principal-is-refused-on-every-vm\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n        [w _] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :foreign]))]\n        [w _] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :foreign]))]\n    (testing \"a module only B vouches for, B declared and A alone trusted:\n              the default interpreter refuses it as untrusted, naming B,\n              raising ImportError in x before e installs\"\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :x])\n                                     (source [a b] [a]))]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= [true false\n                  {:py/out [],\n                   :py/exception\n                   {:type \"ImportError\",\n                    :args [\"Cannot import module 'e': linker refused delivery\"]}}]\n                 outcome)\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str outcome)))\n          (is (= {:status :refused,\n                  :reason :yin.admit/untrusted-principal,\n                  :name 'pym.e,\n                  :yin.admit/decision :refuse,\n                  :yin.admit/asserters [(sign/principal b)]}\n                 (dissoc response :yin.admit/id))\n              (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n          (is (vector? (:yin.admit/id response)) (str k))\n          (observes k nothing-ran seen))\n        w))))\n\n\n(defn- a-trusted-principal-is-allowed-on-every-vm\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n        e (get-in artifact [:units \"e\"])]\n    (testing \"the reader trusts B explicitly: e imports on every VM, its\n              registry entry recording the admission it rode on\"\n      (let [[w results] (on-every-vm w (get-in artifact [:importers :x])\n                                     (source [a b] [a b]))]\n        (doseq [[k [outcome response seen]] results]\n          (is (= caught-e outcome) (str k \" \" (pr-str response)))\n          (observes k {:output [\"caught-e\"],\n                       :guests #{\"pym.e\"},\n                       :children 3,\n                       :admissions {\"pym.e\"\n                                    {:yin.admit/id (:yin.admit/id response),\n                                     :yin.admit/decision :allow,\n                                     :yin.admit/asserters\n                                     [(sign/principal b)],\n                                     :yin.admit/address e}}}\n                    seen))\n        w))))\n\n\n(defn- install-confirmed\n  [follower node events]\n  (reduce (fn [[f n] e]\n            (if (= :confirmed (:yin.head/event e))\n              (let [[f n _] (head/install f n (:principal e) (:trace e))]\n                [f n])\n              [f n]))\n          [follower node]\n          events))\n\n\n(defn- follow-step\n  \"One reading of the world, then one pass of the reader's head\n   follower, installing what it confirms.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [w (step-world w)\n        [f node events] (head/step (:follower w) (:reader w) (:now w))\n        [f node] (install-confirmed f node events)]\n    (assoc w :follower f :reader node)))\n\n\n(defn- move-b-head\n  \"Publish B's next index through the publisher -- B's assertion of\n   pym.e retracted, pym.e now naming `m2` -- deposit its head on B's\n   board, and step the world and the reader's follower until the head is\n   installed: the world.\"\n  [w artifact m2]\n  (let [key-b fixture/key-b\n        pb (sign/principal (:public key-b))\n        [e1] (get-in artifact [:indexes :foreign])\n        signed [(publish/retraction\n                  key-b\n                  {:of (jing/segment-key (:envelope e1)), :seq 2})\n                (publish/assertion key-b\n                                   {:name 'pym.e, :manifest m2, :seq 3})]\n        m (index! (:pub w) signed)\n        w (run-world w 600000 (str \"B's head \" m \" was not reported\")\n                     (published? m))\n        dep (head/deposit! (:board w) key-b m\n                           (index/read-datoms (dht/local (:pub w)) m))\n        limit (+ (:now w) 600000)\n        w (loop [w w]\n            (cond\n              (= m (get (ld/installed-heads (:reader w)) pb)) w\n              (> (:now w) limit) (assoc w :failure \"B's head not installed\")\n              :else (recur (follow-step w))))]\n    (is (= :ok (:status dep)) (pr-str dep))\n    (is (nil? (:failure w)) (:failure w))\n    w))\n\n\n(defn- allow-after-the-head-moves\n  \"The `between` of `run-over-dht` for F1, an external interpreter: it\n   allows each question once, every name but pym.e at once (py is A's),\n   and pym.e only after moving B's head to `m2`. It records under\n   `:asked` every admission id a pending pym.e link names.\"\n  [artifact src m2]\n  (fn [w served]\n    (let [pending (filter :admission (:pending served))\n          e? #(= \"pym.e\" (str (:name %)))\n          w (update w :asked into (map :admission (filter e? pending)))\n          w (if (or (:moved w) (not-any? e? pending))\n              w\n              (let [w (move-b-head w artifact m2)]\n                (is (= m2 (:address (ld/resolve-name (:reader w)\n                                                     (link/authority src)\n                                                     'pym.e)))\n                    \"B's head moved pym.e to M2 while the question was open\")\n                (assoc w :moved true)))]\n      (reduce (fn [w {:keys [admission]}]\n                (if (contains? (:answered w) admission)\n                  w\n                  (do (stream/append! (get-in served\n                                              [:admission :pair :answers])\n                                      {:yin.admit/id admission,\n                                       :yin.admit/decision :allow,\n                                       :yin.admit/conditions {}})\n                      (update w :answered conj admission))))\n              w\n              pending))))\n\n\n(defn- an-allow-binds-the-address-the-question-was-asked-about\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n        pb (sign/principal b)\n        m1 (get-in artifact [:units \"e\"])\n        m2 (get-in artifact [:republished \"k\"])\n        src (source [a b] nil)\n        [f reader] (head/follow (:reader w) {:follow [pb],\n                                             :heads :volatile,\n                                             :poll-ticks 10})\n        board (head/board!)\n        w (assoc w\n                 :reader reader\n                 :follower (head/attach f pb board)\n                 :board board\n                 :asked #{}\n                 :answered #{})]\n    (testing \"M2 is a module the reader has never loaded\"\n      (is (not= m1 m2))\n      (is (nil? (ld/module-status (:reader w) m2))))\n    (testing \"an allow for the question about M1, answered after B's head\n              moved pym.e to M2, links M1 and never fetches M2 (F1)\"\n      (let [[w outcome response seen]\n            (run-over-dht w :semantic (get-in artifact [:importers :x]) src\n                          (allow-after-the-head-moves artifact src m2))\n            id (:yin.admit/id response)]\n        (is (:moved w) \"the question was asked and answered\")\n        (is (= caught-e outcome) (pr-str response))\n        (is (= m1 (:yin.admit/address response)))\n        (is (= (jing/get (dht/local (:pub w)) m1 nil) (:manifest response)))\n        (is (some? (ld/module-status (:reader w) m1)))\n        (is (nil? (ld/module-status (:reader w) m2)))\n        (is (= {\"pym.e\" {:yin.admit/id id,\n                         :yin.admit/decision :allow,\n                         :yin.admit/asserters [pb],\n                         :yin.admit/address m1}}\n               (:admissions seen)))\n        (is (= #{id} (:asked w)) \"the pending admission id never changed\")\n        w))))\n\n\n(defn- site-sets-over-the-mesh\n  \"I7's mesh leg: the reader loads `A`'s site-set index and discovers each\n   unit's record address from the entries `A` signed. It holds no record\n   bytes: the stage load of an import fetches them (`hook-import-with-the-\n   index`). Nothing here prefetches.\"\n  [w artifact]\n  (let [{:keys [a]} (:principals artifact)\n        [w m] (publish-index w (get-in artifact [:indexes :sites]))\n        datoms (dht/loaded-datoms (:reader w) m)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
