{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '160,225p' test/yang/python/antlr/import_programs.cljc && sed -n '50,125p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/siteset.cljc && sed -n '122,180p' test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc && rg -n \\\"runtime.*yang.call|require.*yang.call|noninterruptible\\\" test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_fixture.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"           [:or_test\n            [:and_test\n             [:not_test\n              [:comparison\n               [:expr\n                [:atom_expr\n                 [:atom [:name [\"NAME\" \"print\"]]]\n                 [:trailer\n                  [\"OPEN_PAREN\" \"(\"]\n                  [:arglist\n                   [:argument\n                    [:test\n                     [:or_test\n                      [:and_test\n                       [:not_test\n                        [:comparison\n                         [:expr [:atom_expr [:atom [\"STRING\" \"\\\"m-body\\\"\"]]]]]]]]]]]\n                  [\"CLOSE_PAREN\" \")\"]]]]]]]]]]]]\n       [\"NEWLINE\" \"\\n\"]]]\n     [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]]))\n\n\n(def k-packet\n  \"kval = 3\\nprint(\\\"k-body\\\")\\n\"\n  (packet\n    [:file_input\n     [:stmt\n      [:simple_stmts\n       [:simple_stmt\n        [:expr_stmt\n         [:testlist_star_expr\n          [:test\n           [:or_test\n            [:and_test\n             [:not_test\n              [:comparison [:expr [:atom_expr [:atom [:name [\"NAME\" \"kval\"]]]]]]]]]]]\n         [\"ASSIGN\" \"=\"]\n         [:testlist_star_expr\n          [:test\n           [:or_test\n            [:and_test\n             [:not_test [:comparison [:expr [:atom_expr [:atom [\"NUMBER\" \"3\"]]]]]]]]]]]]\n       [\"NEWLINE\" \"\\n\"]]]\n     [:stmt\n      [:simple_stmts\n       [:simple_stmt\n        [:expr_stmt\n         [:testlist_star_expr\n          [:test\n           [:or_test\n            [:and_test\n             [:not_test\n              [:comparison\n               [:expr\n                [:atom_expr\n                 [:atom [:name [\"NAME\" \"print\"]]]\n                 [:trailer\n                  [\"OPEN_PAREN\" \"(\"]\n                  [:arglist\n                   [:argument\n                    [:test\n                     [:or_test\n                      [:and_test\n                       [:not_test\n                        [:comparison\n                         [:expr [:atom_expr [:atom [\"STRING\" \"\\\"k-body\\\"\"]]]]]]]]]]]\n  {:yang.site/unit :module,\n   :yang.site/prelude :linked,\n   :yang.site/kinds [:call :line :loop]})\n\n\n(def profile-address\n  \"The address the transformation profile is pinned by.\"\n  (jing/segment-key lowering-profile))\n\n\n(defn- medium\n  []\n  :yang.python.antlr/site-set)\n\n\n(defn site-set-of\n  \"`{:root address :tree tree :set [[path mark] ...]}` for the module map\n   AST `ast`: the address of its canonical tree, the tree's rows and its\n   sorted site set.\"\n  [ast]\n  (let [env (encoder/project (encoder/source-envelope\n                               (medium) [:site-set 0] [ast]))\n        tree (nth (:yin/batch env) (:yin/root env))\n        origin (vm/source-origin (:yin/source-medium env)\n                                 (:yin/batch-token env) (:yin/root env))\n        sites (safepoint/sites (:yin/frontend-metadata env) origin (:root tree))]\n    {:root (:root tree), :tree tree, :set (safepoint/site-set sites)}))\n\n\n(defn record\n  \"The publication record associating manifest `manifest` with site set\n   `set-address` over code root `root`.\"\n  [manifest root set-address]\n  {:yang.site/manifest manifest,\n   :yang.site/root root,\n   :yang.site/revision frontend-revision,\n   :yang.site/profile profile-address,\n   :yang.site/set set-address})\n\n\n(defn publish!\n  \"Publish the site set of module `ast` (published at manifest address\n   `manifest`) into `handle`: the set as one blob, then its record. Answers\n   `{:record r :record-address a :set-address s :set [...]}`.\"\n  [handle manifest ast]\n  (let [{:keys [root set]} (site-set-of ast)\n        set-address (jing/materialize! handle (vec set))\n        r (record manifest root set-address)]\n    {:record r,\n     :record-address (jing/materialize! handle r),\n     :set-address set-address,\n     :set set}))\n\n\n(defn- read-at\n  \"The value at `address` in `handle`: `::absent` when the handle holds no\n   bytes for a segment address (the handle is asked with a not-found\n   sentinel, as a byte store is), nil when `address` is no segment address\n   or its bytes do not hash to it, else the value.\"\n  [handle address]\n  (if-not (jing/segment-address? address)\n    nil\n    (let [bs ((:get-bytes-fn handle) address ::absent)]\n      (cond\n        (= ::absent bs) ::absent\n        (nil? bs) ::absent\n        (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs) (jing/segment-value address bs)\n        :else nil))))\n\n\n(defn- absent?\n  [x]\n  (= ::absent x))\n\n\n(defn- missing\n(deftest published-site-sets-verify-test\n  (testing \"every module of the artifact has a site-set record that A's\n            signed index entry publishes, discovered from the published\n            code under A alone, fetched by address, and verifying against\n            the manifest in the artifact's own blobs: root, frontend\n            revision, transformation profile and the set's address (C4\n            slice I7)\"\n    (let [artifact (fixture/read-file)\n          store (mem/create-content-mem (:blobs artifact))\n          datoms (siteset/entry-datoms (get-in artifact [:indexes :sites]))\n          {:keys [a b]} (:principals artifact)\n          hooks {:profile :py/hooks, :hooks true}]\n      (doseq [[n manifest] (artifact-modules artifact)]\n        (let [found (siteset/discover datoms [a] manifest)]\n          (is (= 1 (count found)) n)\n          (is (nil? (siteset/verify store manifest (first found))) n)\n          (is (= :ok (:status (siteset/admit store manifest found hooks))) n)\n          (is (= [] (siteset/discover datoms [b] manifest))\n              (str n \" is not discovered under a principal that did not sign it\"))\n          (is (= :yang.python.antlr/missing-site-set\n                 (:reason (siteset/admit store manifest [] hooks)))\n              n))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The mesh world: a publisher, two plain peers, a reader\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private big\n  \"Every node's inbound bound: py's closure is replicated whole.\"\n  (* 512 1024 1024))\n\n\n(defn- peer-node\n  [net port]\n  (let [c (mesh/join! net port {::jing.dht/publish? true\n                                ::jing.dht/max-inbound-bytes big})]\n    {:composition c, :state (jing.dht/state c)}))\n\n\n(defn- node-at\n  \"A node at mesh `port` whose local store already holds `seed`\n   ({address bytes}): content it has, not content it publishes.\"\n  [net port peer-ports publish? seed]\n  (dht/join {:local (mem/create-content-mem seed),\n             :publish? publish?,\n             :peers (mapv (fn [p] {:host mesh/host, :port p}) peer-ports),\n             :bind! (mesh/seam net port),\n             :max-inbound-bytes big}))\n\n\n(defn- step-world\n  \"One reading: the publisher, the reader when there is one, then every\n   plain peer.\"\n  [w]\n  (let [now (:now w)\n        [pub pub-events] (dht/step (:pub w) now)\n        [reader] (when (:reader w) (dht/step (:reader w) now))]\n    (-> w\ntest/yang/python/antlr/dht_import_test.cljc:72:  {:yin.module/requires {'yang.call :test/call-address}})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The stage code at HEAD already has `yang.call` in the default runtime set at both admission points (`derive-closure` and `stage`), and explicitly bypasses it before site-set lookup. So a `yang.call` missing-set refusal is not coming from that stage unless a caller overrides `:runtime` or the module is emitted under another name. I’m checking the linked wrapper and the committed DHT artifact now; `pym.k` is ordinary guest Python with calls, so it appears intended to carry an instrumentable site set."}}
